#import "template.typ": policy-rule, policy-warning

= Lodging & Hotel Accommodations

== Hotel Selection and Nightly Room Rate Caps

Hotel bookings must be made at reputable business hotels providing clean, secure, and modest accommodations.

#policy-rule("POL-LOD-001", "Nightly Room Rate Caps")[
  Standard single occupancy rooms are the corporate standard. Nightly room rate caps (excluding mandatory local taxes) are structured into two regional tiers:
  - *Tier 1 High-Cost Cities* (New York, London, Zurich, Paris, Tokyo, San Francisco): up to €220.00 / \$250.00 per night.
  - *Tier 2 Standard Business Hubs* (Berlin, Frankfurt, Chicago, Amsterdam, Madrid): up to €160.00 / \$180.00 per night.
  Any booking exceeding these caps requires explicit manager pre-approval attached to the expense claim.
]

== Hotel Incidentals and Minibar Deductions

Hotel bills frequently include non-room charges that must be carefully scrutinized and itemized upon claim submission.

#policy-warning("POL-LOD-002", "Minibar, Spa & Entertainment Disallowance")[
  Charges incurred for hotel minibar beverages or snacks, in-room pay-per-view movies, spa or wellness treatments, fitness center surcharges, and golf or recreational amenities are strictly personal expenses and will be deducted in full from reimbursement.
]

== Laundry and Dry Cleaning Services

#policy-rule("POL-LOD-003", "Extended Stay Laundry Provision")[
  Reasonable laundry and pressing charges are reimbursable exclusively for business trips extending beyond five (5) consecutive business days, up to a maximum limit of €35.00 / \$40.00 per week.
]
